Dear Ruth Castellano,

Thank you for contacting Harbor Credit Union, and I am sorry for the frustration this delay has caused. Your complaint has been logged under reference CMP-2026-0831. We acknowledge every formal complaint within 2 business days and aim to resolve it within 15 business days.

I have confirmed that your wire was held for a routine sanctions screening review, which our policy requires for all international wires, and it was released on 08/21/2026. The beneficiary bank has confirmed receipt. As a courtesy, we have refunded the international wire fee to your account. I also want to explain why we could not tell you about the hold at the time. Screening reviews are confidential while they are open, and staff are not permitted to discuss them until the review is complete. I understand how worrying it is when money for a family member does not arrive as expected, and I have shared your feedback with our Payments Operations team so that we can look at how we set expectations when members send international wires.

If you would like to discuss this further, please reply to this message or call the Member Contact Centre.

Kind regards,

